f32,"kv_optional");return fails;}","notes":"Optional exact --kv-f32 forces type_k and type_v to GGML_TYPE_F32 on separately default-initialized CPU and GPU llama_context_params. With the flag omitted, llama_context_default_params values stay in place and are recorded as requested=default plus actual k/v names. Those three fields enter the workload canon and the JSON requested.kv / kv_requested / kv_actual_k / kv_actual_v fields. Duplicate flags, --kv-f32=1, missing values, and unknown args return bad_arg. Atol 0.01 and rtol 0.01 stay. F16 KV rounding remains a hypothesis; the derived F32 run with GGML_VK_DISABLE_F16=1 still showed 105 of 151936 logit failures. Public headers expose type_k and type_v on llama_context_params and no context readback, so actual means the values passed into each llama_init_from_model. Whitelist, device catalog, tokens 0..15, padded context 256, and prior failure labels stay. Actual child agents: 0. Source patch only; no compile or model run."}
